## Purpose

Move repeatable Tool Shed preparation and closeout mechanics out of model turns and into one thin,
guarded, resumable orchestration surface. Preserve semantic judgment and authority with Codex and
the operator while measuring whether the change actually reduces remedial work, model context, and
retries.

## Desired Outcome

Direct Work1 and Work2 use one compositional runner for deterministic preparation and closeout.
The runner resumes only from exact project and state evidence, preserves current external checks,
returns compact success and bounded failure results, and leaves every underlying command usable on
its own. Local telemetry distinguishes reasoning, deterministic work, recovery, and waiting;
provider-exposed remedial tokens are exact and coverage-labelled, while GUI work uses separate
honest proxies. A sanitized versioned per-project aggregate is ready for IDEA-0007 without making
the hosted dashboard an implementation dependency.

## First Useful Boundary

- Freeze one public orchestration contract and the semantic/authority boundary.
- Define exact-state skip, resume, concurrency, mutation, and recovery behavior.
- Implement and qualify one dry-run/resumable Work1 and Work2 preparation/closeout slice.
- Establish the baseline and prove compact output plus remedial-work reduction.
- Emit and qualify the sanitized per-project reporting aggregate.
- Prove installed-client and maintainer upgrade, rollback, release, and closed-loop reconciliation.

